# `ScopeParent`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`ScopeParent` describes where a [`ScopeBoundary`](./ScopeBoundary) may be opened. `Root` names the framework-owned application root. `of::<T>()` names another static scope type declared by the same [`ScopeTopology`](./ScopeTopology); `boundary` provides the equivalent identity-based form.

The parent must be present in the topology unless it is `Root`, and it must have a lower, longer-lived rank than its child. These checks establish the containment rules that runtime scope opening and dependency validation use.

Choose the immediate transport containment relationship, not an arbitrary scope that happens to be longer lived. A request scope nested inside a connection should name the connection boundary; a connection scope should name `Root`.

